WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.500
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:20.310
Rental Magica

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:28.350
The shadow of the moon as it waxes and wanes...
Michikakeru tsuki no kage sotto

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:38.030
...gently stirs the beat of sorrow in your heart.
kanashimi no kodou furuwasu

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.730
Its wandering attraction...
Samayou inryoku

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:47.670
...reflected in your eyes.
hitomi ni utsushite

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:53.650
You will surpass the darkness of Ioneliness.
Kodoku no yami wo koeteyuku

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:59.350
You know that truth in your heart.
Shinjitsu wa kono mune ni

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:05.030
That gentleness will become your strength.
Yasashisa wa tsuyosa ni naru

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.660
Don't be afraid. Believe.
Osorenaide shinjiru koto

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.500
The brilliance that blooms in the cosmos eternally...
Sora ni saku kirameki wa towa ni

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:19.470
...embraces the voice of time.
toki no koe dakishime

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.540
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.280
Let me hear.
Kikasete

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.020
Wind, speak to me.
Kaze tsutaete

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:40.520
Tell me what courage is.
Yuuki wo

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.370
There's a tiny bit of spell wave
contamination to the southwest...

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.960
...which is disrupting the ley line.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.730
It looks like The Association has already
given this job to Astral, though.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.080
Let's have our Goetia company bid on this, too.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.710
There's absolutely no room
for failure in this plan.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:10.480
"Spell wave contamination" is the magic
equivalent of radioactive contamination.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.300
It's the degeneration of objects
or living creatures...

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.320
...contaminated by evil spell power.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.870
For example, it could lead
to something rotting away,

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.560
or being possessed by an evil spirit,
or a mind becoming diseased.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.290
I... cchan?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:56.000
NO!!!

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:03.710
Festival! Festival! Gonna have some fun!

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.680
Oh, jeez!

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.840
Oh, dear. Excuse me.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.690
Isn't it a little out of place to
celebrate Boy's Day in a mage's office?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.250
Not at all, Mr. President.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.760
It's said odd double-number dates like
5/5 and 7/7 reinforce each other and,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.390
conversely, summon evil powers.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.430
Look, this "Mr. President" stuff...

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.510
To drive away that evil power,

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.240
you decorate a place like this
with dolls and armor and helmets.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.440
Magic like this for controlling spell power
is called semantic magic, Mr. President.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.680
As I was saying, this Mr. President stuff...

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:47.120
In England, 11/1 is a festival
to mark the coming of winter.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.810
Miss Honami?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.420
Big Sister Honami!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.690
Episode 2
A WITCH'S VOW

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:57.600
Encyclopedia of the Celts

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.040
Encyclopedia of the Celts
According to Celtic tradition, on the eve of the
festival, the night we know as Halloween,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.300
According to Celtic tradition, on the eve of the
festival, the night we know as Halloween,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.430
faeries turn evil and kidnap
children and young girls.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.040
K-Kidnap?

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:14.910
Reinforcement. In short, as good fortune
is multiplied, it brings happiness.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.450
But, conversely, it draws the
other world closer to our own.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:31.460
And once you know about the other world,
you come back changed by it in some way.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:38.030
Which is why I shouldn't be your president!

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.670
I know! Why don't you be the
president, Mr. Nekoyashiki?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.740
It's The Association's decision.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.410
Only you, the only son of the last
president, can be his successor.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.610
If you don't do it, the company
will fall apart, Brother Pres.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:59.090
And if that happens, tomorrow we'll
all be wandering the roadside.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.530
Even saying that...

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:08.400
I don't think Iba's cut out to
be president. He's not a mage.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.270
Mage Recruiting Agency
ASTRAL
We rent mages to meet your demands.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:32.390
And once you know about the other world,
you come back changed by it in some way.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.320
Why do I wish I hadn't heard that?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.990
Itsuki Iba, I presume.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.140
H-How do you know my name?

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.480
You're Astral's second generation president?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.780
Then, are you a mage, too?

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:34.620
My name is Adelicia Lenn Mathers,
and I run the Goetia company.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.080
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.750
Goet?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.290
Don't tell me you've never heard of Goetia.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.160
Um, well...

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.240
You're telling me you've never heard of Goetia,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.600
the oldest and most
respected of magical groups?!

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.240
That you've never heard of the Mathers family,

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.110
who have possessed the Seal of
Solomon since time immemorial?!

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.910
Yeah. Sorry!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.850
You're just the president
in name only, aren't you?

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.890
Well, knowing that, now I don't
have to waste any time with you.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:15.230
Anyway, just hand over the
contract Astral's been given to me.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.290
Contract? What do you mean?

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.360
What, you don't know what a contract is, either?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:29.880
Just sign this document and it'll be all set.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:34.850
But, this'll be my responsibility.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:41.750
Besides, I don't think I should do
anything that might hurt Astral.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:46.020
I see. Then let me help you.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.890
Come forth, Botis!
The wise count who rules 60 legions!

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.870
Now then, if you would be so kind.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.010
I just can't, really!

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:08.950
Botis!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.230
Miss Honami?

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:27.260
You've got a long way to go before you can
summon all 72 demons, don't you, Addie?

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.300
Don't call me by that overly-familiar
nickname you gave me, Honami.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:35.470
Um... Are you two friends?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.770
Don't be ridiculous!
Don't be ridiculous!

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.620
Addie, why did you come all
the way here from England?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.190
I don't have to tell you.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:49.550
Fine. I don't really care. However...

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.590
Capturing this newbie and trying
to force him to sign is really low.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.360
Isn't that a disgrace to the name of Goetia?

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:02.940
So, Astral admits the disgrace of
putting this amateur in charge?!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.770
Look, if you want to settle things
here and now, I'm up for it!

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.310
Sounds like fun!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.440
You two shouldn't fight like this!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.080
Very well. In deference to the new president,

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:19.450
I shall allow Astral to demonstrate its skill here.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.280
Forneus!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.410
Scattering spell power like that around...

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.670
She probably doesn't even care about the
spell wave contamination she may cause.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.600
W-What?

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.470
You're bleeding.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.010
I'm fine. It doesn't even hurt anymore.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:21.740
When you're really sensitive,
spell power can end up blinding you.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.180
Be careful.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.810
R... Really?

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.520
So, what do we do now?

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:29.750
What do you mean?

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.320
About Astral.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:40.120
I don't think you should force yourself
to be the president if you don't want to.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.060
I doubt you can do the job
if your heart's not in it.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:51.310
Well... You have some time to think it over.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.470
Oh, I almost forgot!

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:55.870
Here.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.420
I came to give this to you from Nekoyashiki.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.920
Astral's company badge.

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.910
You can have it for now.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:05.690
Miss Honami!

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.250
"Miss Honami."

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.030
You really don't remember at all, do you?

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.370
Just plain Honami, please.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.150
H-Hello?

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:08.120
Mr. President?

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:09.610
Mr. Nekoyashiki?

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.390
Could you please head directly to the job site?

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.950
T... The job site? What's up?

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.390
It's just a simple spell wave decontamination.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:20.130
But, it's night time! It's pitch black out!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.240
I probably shouldn't say this,

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:27.640
but Honami said you'd just get in the
way if you went and tried to stop her.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:38.190
I'm afraid that tonight's our
occult magazine's deadline...

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.420
...and I can't go out there myself.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.720
It's spell wave contamination,
but nothing major.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.390
I don't see why Goetia was in such
a sweat to get this contract from us.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:13.880
Scared?

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.760
I'm okay. I'm a mage, after all.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:19.730
Huh?

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.490
Besides, you're special, aren't you, Icchan?

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:26.800
Come on, let's go.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.650
It's the same as that time before?

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:44.790
What is this?

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:47.980
Is my own mind somehow amplifying
the spell wave contamination?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.120
It's trying to turn the
hunter into the hunted, huh?

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.520
As if!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.270
What? Miss Honami!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.440
Boss? Why are you?!

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:14.110
Um, well, Mr. Nekoyashiki told me...

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.770
I told him we didn't need you here.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.790
Does your right eye hurt?

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:22.790
I'm fine.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:23.980
No, you're not!

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.490
I'll be fine by myself. Go back.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.560
I can't do that to you!

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.660
Besides, isn't this land supposed to be vacant?

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:34.230
Is this that, what do you call it?

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:37.630
S... S... Spell wave contamination?

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:41.170
And I'm telling you, your being
here won't help me with this.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.310
Weren't you the one who said he didn't
want to be the president in the first place?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.580
Yeah, but still...

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:51.550
Icchan?!

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:54.250
Icchan!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.290
That's why I told him to go back!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:08.760
Icchan!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.400
Where are you?!

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.180
Why does this always happen to him?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.670
Miss Honami?

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:24.250
Miss Honami? Honami!

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:27.980
Honami?

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:59.380
So, even a ghost horse has
trouble going up stairs. Lucky!

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.120
Icchan is always...

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:27.780
I... cchan?

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:32.520
Over here! Catch me if you can!

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:41.950
Don't... DON'T!!!

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:45.330
Why?

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.460
Why did I endure that strict training?

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.500
Why was I so desperate to learn magic?

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.700
Here! I can hide here for now!

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.320
Why do I have to deal with stuff like this?!

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:20.330
Um, shouldn't you be with your horse?

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:28.900
Let me guess.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:33.210
A headless knight who's
looking for a head, right?

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:43.150
I'm your dance partner, pal.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:45.850
Honami!

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:49.360
I... I'm your prey!

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.290
Y-Y-You're looking for a head, right?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:57.960
Icchan...

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.300
Even scared to death, you're still reckless.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:06.900
Come on, a bird in the hand
is worth two in the bush!

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.910
I-I-I think having a choice is overrated, anyway!

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:14.550
That part of you hasn't
changed a bit from that time.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.520
But I'm not the girl I was!

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:19.860
I'm the one you're fighting!

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.220
Or don't you have the guts?!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:35.740
I...

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:38.580
Icchan...

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:41.940
DON'T!!!

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.060
Icchan?

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:05.700
Icchan?

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:14.040
NO!!!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.750
I'm not that girl anymore!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.660
With the divine protection of the mistletoe
which dwells in neither Heaven nor Earth,

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.350
pierce through the calamity to the northwest!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:25.680
Hail!

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.640
Thank goodness.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:56.920
I'm sorry for not being any help.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:19:59.990
Icchan!

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.700
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:21.780
I came here to protect you, Icchan.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:46.200
Spell wave decontamination, complete.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.240
You've saved Goetia some work.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.300
Good job, Honami.

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:01.120
May
11th

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.990
And spell wave contamination is?

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:05.960
Um... Uh, let's see...

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.000
Do it without checking the notebook for once!

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.590
Right! Why so strict all of a sudden?

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.630
You said you wanted to be the president, right?

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:17.400
In that case, I'm gonna tutor you till you drop!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.370
Huh?!

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.610
How do you do, everyone?

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:30.510
My name is Adelicia Lenn Mathers.

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.780
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:34.820
Addie...

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:47.530
The next bid's going to Goetia... Itsuki.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.110
Hey!

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:54.770
Eyes on me, pal.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:56.500
R-Right.

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:08.110
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:16.520
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:29.570
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:41.490
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.760
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:52.270
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:56.540
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:01.630
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:02.580 --> 00:23:13.510
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:13.890 --> 00:23:17.560
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:21.790
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.890
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.330
Saniwa [SANIWA]

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:30.370
Saniwa [SANIWA]
A saniwa is a person who can
hear the judgment of a god.

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:33.070
Saniwa [SANIWA]
You have to be sure of what sort of god
manifests in a shrine maiden, though.

00:23:33.070 --> 00:23:34.210
You have to be sure of what sort of god
manifests in a shrine maiden, though.

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:36.210
Wow. I'd like to interview them!

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:38.300
Well, as long as you understand that much.

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:39.910
Is that all for today, Prof. Miwa?

00:23:39.910 --> 00:23:40.410
Next
Time
"Purification of
the Gods"
Is that all for today, Prof. Miwa?

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:41.180
Next
Time
"Purification of
the Gods"
Okay.
